#
# valgrind.supp — Valgrind Memcheck suppressions for known external-library
# false positives.
#
# Only libraries outside the ntrickle project (libc, libstdc++, libevent,
# dlopen, ld-linux) may be suppressed here.  Never suppress project-owned
# allocations, leaks, or invalid accesses.
#
# This file is intentionally minimal.  Suppressions are added only when a
# confirmed external-library issue cannot be addressed otherwise.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# libevent: event_base initialisation allocates internal data structures
# (eventfd pairs, timer queues, I/O multiplexing backends) that are freed
# implicitly when the process exits.  Under Valgrind these appear as
# "still reachable" or as fds not explicitly closed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dlopen / ld-linux: the dynamic linker caches symbol resolution tables
# and shared-object handles.  These are internal to the runtime linker and
# are not freed by the application.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
